.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/
.env
.DS_Store

# nflverse feeds are large and reproducible from their release assets, so every
# cache directory is ignored and the two that are committed are named: the
# schedule because the credit arithmetic must stay re-checkable, and the probe
# cache because it is bought evidence.
#
# This was an enumeration of seven directories until 2026-09-07, which meant a
# feed added later was not ignored at all. Several Claude sessions share this
# checkout and `git add -A` from any of them has swept another's files into a
# commit twice; `participation` is 47 MB a season. A rule that has to be
# extended by hand for each new feed is a rule that is one feed from wrong.
data/raw/nfl/*/
!data/raw/nfl/schedules/
!data/raw/nfl/historical_probe/
data/processed/*.csv

# Single-season backtest bets. `run_props_backtest.py` writes one of these per
# season; the pooled `*_props_backtest_bets.csv` that four reports read comes
# only from `run_props_replication.py`. They shared a filename until
# 2026-08-31, and a partial set of season files committed alongside the pooled
# one is the same confusion in a different shape.
data/outputs/*_props_backtest_bets_[0-9]*.csv
